              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.553,
            0.883,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. One plate of Jowar roti costs ₹30 and one plate of Pulao costs ₹20. If x plates of Jowar roti and y plates of pulao were ordered in a day, which expression(s) describe the total amount in rupees earned that day? (a) 30x + 20y",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\begin{aligned} &(30 + 20) \\times (x + y)\\\\ &30x - 20y\\\\ \\end{aligned}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) 20x + 30y",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (d) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(30 + 20) \\times x + y"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (e)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.665,
            0.297,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (a) 30x + 20y."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.701,
            0.883,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Pushpita sells two types of flowers on Independence Day: champak and marigold. ‘p’ customers only bought champak, ‘q’ customers only bought marigold, and ‘r’ customers bought both. On the same day, she gave away a tiny national flag to every customer. How many flags did she give away that day?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (a) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pmb { p } + \\pmb { q } + \\pmb { r }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\pmb { p } + \\pmb { q } + 2 \\pmb { r }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (c) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times ( \\boldsymbol{p} + \\boldsymbol{q} + \\boldsymbol{r} )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (d) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p + q + r + 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (e) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\boldsymbol{p}+\\boldsymbol{q}+\\boldsymbol{r}+\\boldsymbol{1}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (f) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times ( \\pmb { p } + \\pmb { q } )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
